36C430 633 466 620 493 602C545 567 575 516 586 442C591 416 593 377 593 338C593 226 575 145 515 95C466 55 423 46 339 46C297 46 248 47 244 48C238 49 233 53 232 59C231 62 231 143 231 344C231 622 232 625 234 628C236 632 241 635 250 636C256 636 289 637 322 637C355 637 389 636 395 636Z\"></path></defs></svg>","mathFallback":false,"description":"JEE Main's 2021 JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift Paper's All Questions with solutions provider ExamSIDE.Com","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift","nextq":"3h9rsgxff6fwc92zST1klt2rjao","prevq":"ssDfoVbytyEM2abSbb1klt249qz","questions":[{"question_id":"SrNQK9wS3AmWrLIZ9e1klt2g8bl","chapter":"wave-optics","chapterGroup":"optics","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift","permalink":"consider-the-diffraction-pattern-obtained-from-the-sunlight-jee-main-physics-units-and-measurements-kaq2k2vtytl2omez","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Consider the diffraction pattern obtained from the sunlight incident on a pinhole of diameter 0.1 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.364ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 603 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>m. If the diameter of the pinhole is slightly increased, it will affect the diffraction pattern such that:","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"its size increases, but intensity decreases"},{"identifier":"B","content":"its size increases, and intensity increases"},{"identifier":"C","content":"its size decreases, but intensity increases"},{"identifier":"D","content":"its sizes decreases, and intensity decreases"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Yes, you're absolutely correct. This equation you provided is for the angular size of the central maximum (or central diffraction disk) in a circular aperture diffraction pattern (like a pinhole) :</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.006ex\" height=\"2.782ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -884.7 5306.7 1229.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"69\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-69\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(672,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1228,0)\"><use data-c=\"2061\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2061\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1394.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2141.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(3197.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1778,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(762,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D437\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D437\"></use></g><rect width=\"1869.5\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>where :</p>\n<ul>\n<li>θ is the angle subtended by the radius of the central maximum at the pinhole,</li>\n<br><li>λ is the wavelength of the light, and</li>\n<br><li>D is the diameter of the aperture or pinhole.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If D (the diameter of the pinhole) is increased, then sinθ (and hence θ itself, for small θ) will decrease, implying that the size of the central maximum or diffraction disk will decrease. This is because less diffraction (bending of light) occurs when the pinhole is larger.</p>\n<p>At the same time, increasing the size of the pinhole allows more light to pass through, which increases the intensity (brightness) of the light in the diffraction pattern.</p>\n<p>So, increasing the diameter of the pinhole decreases the size of the diffraction pattern but increases its intensity, which confirms Option C.</p>\n"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.498ex\" height=\"2.186ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 3314 966\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\"> </text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1878,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D707\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D707\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2481,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> व्यास के किसी सुईछित्र द्वारा प्राप्त उस विवर्तन पैटर्न पर विचार कीजिए जो सूर्य के प्रकाश के आपतित होने पर बनता है। यदि इस सुईछित्र के व्यास में थोड़ी वृद्धि कर दें, तो यह विवर्तन स्वरूप को इस प्रकार प्रभाव्ति करेगा कि विवर्तन स्वरूप के</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"आकार में वृद्धि होगी परन्तु तीव्रता से घटेगी"},{"identifier":"B","content":"आकार में घटेगा तथा तीव्रता घटेगी"},{"identifier":"C","content":"आकार में घटेगा परन्तु तीव्रता से वृद्धि होगी"},{"identifier":"D","content":"आकार में वृद्धि तथा तीव्रता वृद्धि होगी"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>यह समीकरण आपके द्वारा प्रदान किया गया है, यह एक वृत्ताकार छिद्र डिफ्रैक्शन पैटर्न (जैसे कि एक पिनहोल) में केंद्रीय अधिकतम (या केंद्रीय डिफ्रैक्शन डिस्क) के कोणीय आकार के लिए है:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.006ex\" height=\"2.782ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -884.7 5306.7 1229.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"73\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-73\"></use><use data-c=\"69\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-69\" transform=\"translate(394,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"6E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6E\" transform=\"translate(672,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1228,0)\"><use data-c=\"2061\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2061\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1394.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2141.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(3197.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1778,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(762,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D437\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D437\"></use></g><rect width=\"1869.5\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>जहां :</p>\n<ul>\n<li>θ वह कोण है जिसका पिनहोल पर केंद्रीय अधिकतम की त्रिज्या द्वारा उपनिबंधित किया जाता है,</li>\n<br><li>λ प्रकाश की तरंगदैर्ध्य है, और</li>\n<br><li>D छिद्र या पिनहोल का व्यास है।</li>\n</ul>\n<p>यदि D (पिनहोल का व्यास) बढ़ाया जाता है, तो sinθ (और इसके फलस्वरूप θ स्वयं, छोटे θ के लिए) कम हो जाएगा, जिसका अर्थ है कि केंद्रीय अधिकतम या डिफ्रैक्शन डिस्क का आकार कम हो जाएगा। यह इसलिए होता है क्योंकि पिनहोल जब बड़ा होता है, तो प्रकाश की डिफ्रैक्शन (प्रकाश के मोड़) कम होती है।</p>\n<p>एक ही समय में, पिनहोल के आकार को बढ़ाने से अधिक प्रकाश होता है, जो डिफ्रैक्शन पैटर्न में प्रकाश की तीव्रता (चमक) को बढ़ाता है।</p>\n"}},"subject":"physics","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"diffraction-and-doppler-effect-of-light","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-25th-february-evening-slot","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-25th-february-evening-slot","active":true},{"question_id":"zkHpx5JygAuEDEZmFm1klt2hx0y","chapter":"magnetic-properties-of-matter","chapterGroup":"electricity","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift","permalink":"in-a-ferromagnetic-material-below-the-curie-temperature-a-jee-main-physics-units-and-measurements-zehae6pttutl40g1","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"In a ferromagnetic material, below the curie temperature, a domain is defined as :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"a macroscopic region with zero magnetization."},{"identifier":"B","content":"a macroscopic region with saturation magnetization."},{"identifier":"C","content":"a macroscopic region with randomly oriented magnetic dipoles."},{"identifier":"D","content":"a macroscopic region with consecutive magnetic dipoles oriented in opposite direction."}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"In a ferromagnetic material, below the curie temperature a domain is defined as a macroscopic region with saturation magnetization."},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>क्यूरी-ताप से नीचे किसी लौह-चुम्बकीय पदार्थ के डोमेन को इस रूप में परिभाषित किया जाता है</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"विपरीत दिशा में अभिविन्यासित क्रमागत चुम्बकीय द्विध्रुवों का कोई स्थूल क्षेत्र"},{"identifier":"B","content":"संतृप्त चुम्बकन का कोई स्थूल क्षेत्र"},{"identifier":"C","content":"सादृच्छिक अभिविन्यासित चुम्बकीय द्विध्रुवों का कोई स्थूल क्षेत्र"},{"identifier":"D","content":"शून्य चुम्बकन का कोई स्थूल क्षेत्र"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":null}},"subject":"physics","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"magnetic-properties-of-matter","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-25th-february-evening-slot","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-25th-february-evening-slot","active":true},{"question_id":"PesjmeqFYD1rQtwYSH1klt2kqz5","chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"mechanics","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift","permalink":"given-below-are-two-statements-brbrstatement-i--in-a-jee-main-physics-units-and-measurements-xsyfwq8ht7hnw9yd","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Given below are two statements :<br><br>Statement I : In a diatomic molecule, the rotational energy at a given temperature obeys Maxwell's distribution.<br><br>Statement II : In a diatomic molecule, the rotational energy at a given temperature equals the translational kinetic energy for each molecule.<br><br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true."}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"The translational kinetic energy &amp; rotational kinetic energy both obey Maxwell's distribution independent of each other.<br><br>T.K.E. of diatomic molecules = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.596ex\" height=\"2.736ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.2 2031.6 1209.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(793.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1314.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><br><br>R.K.E. of diatomic molecules = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.596ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 2031.6 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(793.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1314.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><br><br>So statement I is true but statement II is false."},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>कथन I किसी द्वि-परमाणुक अणु में किसी दिए गए ताप पर घूर्णन-ऊर्जा मैक्सवेल वितरण का पालन करती है।</p>\n<p>कथन II किसी द्वि-परमाणुक अणु में प्रत्येक अणु के लिए किसी दिए गए ताप पर घूर्णन ऊर्जा रै��िक गतिज ऊर्जा के बराबर होती है।</p>\n<p>उपरोक्त कथनों के सन्दर्भ में नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सबसे उचित उत्तर चुनिए</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"दोनों कथन I और कथन II सही नहीं हैं।"},{"identifier":"B","content":"कथन I सही नहीं है परन्तु कथन II सही है।"},{"identifier":"C","content":"कथन I सही है परन्तु कथन II सही नहीं है।"},{"identifier":"D","content":"दोनों कथन I और कथन II सही हैं।"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":null}},"subject":"physics","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"degree-of-freedom-and-law-of-equipartition-of-energy","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-25th-february-evening-slot","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-25th-february-evening-slot","active":true},{"question_id":"8OGOKavxUO7OfLwZaI1klt2p82o","chapter":"alternating-current","chapterGroup":"electricity","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift","permalink":"match-list-i-with-list-iibrbrtable-thead-tr-jee-main-physics-units-and-measurements-bnnnunofnie2tluz","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Match List I with List II.<br><br><table>\n<thead>\n  <tr>\n    <th></th>\n    <th>List I</th>\n    <th></th>\n    <th>List II</th>\n  </tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(a)</td>\n    <td>Rectifier</td>\n    <td>(i)</td>\n    <td>Used either for stepping up or stepping down the a.c. voltage</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(b)</td>\n    <td>Stabilizer</td>\n    <td>(ii)</td>\n    <td>Used to convert a.c. voltage into d.c. voltage</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(c)</td>\n    <td>Transformer</td>\n    <td>(iii)</td>\n    <td>Used to remove any ripple in the rectified output voltage</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(d)</td>\n    <td>Filter</td>\n    <td>(iv)</td>\n    <td>Used for constant output voltage even when the input voltage or load current change</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><br><br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)"},{"identifier":"B","content":"(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"},{"identifier":"C","content":"(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)"},{"identifier":"D","content":"(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"(a) Rectifier : used to convert a a.c. voltage into d.c. voltage.<br><br>(b) Stabilizer : used for constant output voltage even when the input voltage or load current change<br><br>(c) Transformer : used either for stepping up or stepping down the a.c. voltage.<br><br>(d) Filter : used to remove any ripple in the rectified output voltage."},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>सूची I और सूची II को मिलाइए।</p>\n<p>\n<table class=\"tg\" style=\"undefined;table-layout: fixed; width: 549px\">\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 44px\">\n<col style=\"width: 86px\">\n<col style=\"width: 52px\">\n<col style=\"width: 367px\">\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n  <tr>\n    <th class=\"tg-amwm\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-amwm\">सूची I</th>\n    <th class=\"tg-amwm\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-amwm\">सूची II</th>\n  </tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">(A)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">दिष्टकारी</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">1.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.048ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.33ex\" height=\"1.667ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 1472 737\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> वोल्टता को उपचायी अथवा अपचायी करने में उपयोगी</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">(B)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">स्थायीकारी</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">2.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.048ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.33ex\" height=\"1.667ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 1472 737\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> वोल्टता को <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.048ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.362ex\" height=\"1.643ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1486 726\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"44\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-44\"></use><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\" transform=\"translate(764,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> वोल्टता में परिवर्तित करने में उपयोगी</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">(C)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">ट्रांसफॉर्मर</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">3.</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">दिष्टकृत निर्गत वोल्टता की उर्मिकाओं को हटाने में उपयोगी</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">(D)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">फिल्टर</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\">4.</td